<title>THAILAND: Thai grains discharge schedule for Feb 19.</title>
<headline>Thai grains discharge schedule for Feb 19.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed grains discharges at Thai ports as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>Vessel	   Date of Arrival     Commodity	    Amount</p>
<p>Dali	     Feb 02	     IND groundnut meal    8,476</p>
<p>					  IND soymeal	     7,800</p>
<p>Gan Jiang	Feb 06	     IND soymeal	     7,414</p>
<p>					  IND groundnut meal    4,252</p>
<p>Hallard	  Feb 08	     IND soymeal	    13,640</p>
<p>Zi Yun	   Feb 10	     IND oymeal	     6,000</p>
<p>Feng Tao	 Feb 13	     IND soymeal	    11,153</p>
<p>CSK Glory	Feb 13	     US soybeans	    16,031</p>
<p>					  US soymeal	     37,086</p>
<p>Sincere Olympus Feb 17	    Canadian wheat	  5,999</p>
<p>Song Shan	Feb 22	     IND groundnut	   3,100</p>
<p>					  IND soymeal	     6,324</p>
<p>					  IND rapeseed	    2,026</p>
<p>C Tausin	 Feb 27	     US soybeans	    47,849</p>
<p>Sin HUng I     end-Feb	    IND soymeal,</p>
<p>					  groundnut meal	 12,000</p>
<p>Lissom	   mid-Mar	    ARG &amp; BRZ soymeal    20,000</p>
<p>NOTE: IND is abbreviation for INDIA.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
